Privacy Policy for The Found Merchant

Effective Date: July 17, 2026

The Found Merchant is a Chrome extension that enhances supported D&D Beyond character sheets by providing a Dungeon Master-controlled merchant and inventory system for tabletop roleplaying campaigns.

Information Used by the Extension

To provide its functionality, the extension accesses game-related information displayed on supported D&D Beyond character sheets. This may include a character's name, portrait, race, class, level, currency, and inventory.

The extension also processes merchant information, storefront inventories, purchases, sales, receipts, and session ledger data created while using the extension.

The Found Merchant does not collect personal information such as names, email addresses, passwords, financial information, browsing history, location data, or personal communications.

How Information Is Used

The information accessed by the extension is used solely to:

Identify the active D&D Beyond character.
Display available merchant inventories.
Calculate purchases and sales.
Track merchant inventory and storefront status.
Synchronize the active shopping session between the Dungeon Master and participating players.

The information is not used for advertising, profiling, analytics, or any purpose unrelated to the operation of the extension.

Storage and Synchronization

Extension preferences and local configuration are stored using Chrome Extension Storage.

Merchant inventories, storefront state, transaction history, and other campaign data may be synchronized using Google Firebase Firestore so that participating players and the Dungeon Master share the same shopping session.

Only the information necessary to operate the merchant system is synchronized.

Data Sharing

The Found Merchant does not sell, rent, or transfer user information to third parties.

Data is shared only with Google Firebase/Firestore as the hosting platform required to synchronize campaign merchant data between participants. Google processes this data in accordance with its own privacy policies.

Analytics and Advertising

The Found Merchant does not include:

Advertising
Analytics
User tracking
Behavioral profiling
Marketing services
Data Retention

Campaign data remains available until it is removed by the Dungeon Master, deleted from browser storage, or deleted from the associated Firebase/Firestore project.

Security

Reasonable efforts are made to protect stored and transmitted information and to request only the permissions required for the extension's operation. No method of electronic storage or transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure.

Children's Privacy

The Found Merchant is intended for tabletop roleplaying participants and is not directed toward children under the age of 13. The extension does not knowingly collect personal information from children.

Changes to This Policy

This Privacy Policy may be updated as the extension evolves. The Effective Date at the top of this document will be revised whenever material changes are made.

Contact

Questions regarding this Privacy Policy may be directed to the extension developer using the contact information provided on the Chrome Web Store developer listing.
